Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 20:13:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Review: the np 3 run tests the sliver warning's
 reduction; a missing dump directory keeps the refusal's reason

- tests/parallel/test_0907 says np 3 is the run whose surgery is off rank 0,
  and scripts/test.sh runs it at np 3 always.
- When UW_PLACE_FILL_DUMP names a directory the dump cannot be written to,
  the refusal keeps its own reason and adds why the dump failed.
- The design note says where the dump goes.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
---
 .../design/fault-parallel-placement-2026-09.md |  3 ++-
 scripts/test.sh                                |  5 +++++
 src/underworld3/utilities/place_surface.py     | 18 +++++++++++-------
 ...est_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py |  9 +++++----
 4 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/developer/design/fault-parallel-placement-2026-09.md b/docs/developer/design/fault-parallel-placement-2026-09.md
index b10556fc..81a1877c 100644
--- a/docs/developer/design/fault-parallel-placement-2026-09.md
+++ b/docs/developer/design/fault-parallel-placement-2026-09.md
@@ -758,7 +758,8 @@ band along strike (its vertices are all victims and the two fills have
 no common boundary to keep); a crossing so oblique that the skin
 changes hands at fewer than two vertices; and 3-D, where the thin volume
 still gathers. A refused fill saves its inputs to
-`place_fill_failure_rank<r>.npz` beside the script.
+`place_fill_failure_rank<r>.npz` in the directory named by `UW_PLACE_FILL_DUMP`, when
+that is set.
 
 ### The fill graded harder (4 September)
 
diff --git a/scripts/test.sh b/scripts/test.sh
index ec35dd50..048c5289 100755
--- a/scripts/test.sh
+++ b/scripts/test.sh
@@ -713,6 +713,11 @@ if [ $PARALLEL_RANKS -gt 0 ] && shard_owns 6 && command -v mpirun &> /dev/null;
     OMPI_MCA_rmaps_base_oversubscribe=1 $SUPERVISE mpirun -n 3 python -m pytest --with-mpi \
       tests/parallel/test_0786_stokes_rank_without_cells_parallel.py || status=1
 
+    # At three ranks the outcrop's surgery runs on a rank that is not rank 0, so the
+    # sliver warning's reduction over the ranks is exercised; at two it is not.
+    OMPI_MCA_rmaps_base_oversubscribe=1 $SUPERVISE mpirun -n 3 python -m pytest --with-mpi \
+      tests/parallel/test_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py || status=1
+
     # The parallel plotting helpers: the non-plotting ranks join the plotting
     # rank's global_evaluate with no points; at three ranks two of them do.
     OMPI_MCA_rmaps_base_oversubscribe=1 $SUPERVISE mpirun -n 3 python -m pytest --with-mpi \
diff --git a/src/underworld3/utilities/place_surface.py b/src/underworld3/utilities/place_surface.py
index f4fb669a..85b83501 100644
--- a/src/underworld3/utilities/place_surface.py
+++ b/src/underworld3/utilities/place_surface.py
@@ -8180,13 +8180,17 @@ def _place_thin_volume_2d(dm, polylines, width, label, label_value,
                     if dump_dir:
                         dump = _os.path.join(
                             dump_dir, f"place_fill_failure_rank{comm.rank}.npz")
-                        np.savez(dump, Xall=Xall, ring=np.asarray(ring),
-                                 holes=np.asarray(
-                                     [len(h) for h in holes] + sum(
-                                         ([int(v) for v in h] for h in holes),
-                                         [])),
-                                 seams=str(seams))
-                        where = f"fill inputs saved to {dump}"
+                        try:
+                            np.savez(dump, Xall=Xall, ring=np.asarray(ring),
+                                     holes=np.asarray(
+                                         [len(h) for h in holes] + sum(
+                                             ([int(v) for v in h] for h in holes),
+                                             [])),
+                                     seams=str(seams))
+                            where = f"fill inputs saved to {dump}"
+                        except OSError as save_error:
+                            # the refusal's own reason leads; the dump only adds
+                            where = f"the fill inputs could not be saved to {dump}: {save_error}"
                     else:
                         where = ("set UW_PLACE_FILL_DUMP to a directory to save the "
                                  "fill inputs")
diff --git a/tests/parallel/test_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py b/tests/parallel/test_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py
index a28b5b5c..cb611ad0 100644
--- a/tests/parallel/test_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py
+++ b/tests/parallel/test_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py
@@ -2,11 +2,12 @@
 
 The smallest angle where an outcropping band meets the wall is a minimum over the
 ranks, so it is the same on every rank even when only one of them holds wall cells;
-the warning is printed once (rank 0). With the top at 63.5 degrees on this annulus
-the outcrop's surgery runs on rank 1 at np 2, so rank 0 holds no wall cell of it and
-would report 180 without the reduction.
+the warning is printed once (rank 0). At np 2 rank 0 holds the band, so the run
+checks agreement and the single print. At np 3, with the top at 63.5 degrees on this
+annulus, the outcrop's surgery runs on a rank other than 0, which would report 180
+without the reduction: that run, always on in scripts/test.sh, is the one that tests it.
 
-    mpirun -n 2 python -m pytest --with-mpi tests/parallel/test_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py
+    mpirun -n 3 python -m pytest --with-mpi tests/parallel/test_0907_outcrop_sliver_warning_parallel.py
 """
 import numpy as np
 import pytest
